- Constraint 1: 0 of 12 off-topic questions end only-weak (LEAF-IR's score scale differs; its catalog floor is 0.3 vs Granite's 0.78).
- Constraint 2: Q08 gets a false only-weak note.
- Gates: LEAF-IR's own ranking misses Q14 within 3 searches (30/31). The strength rule does not rank, so this is the model, not the rule (see API/E2E F-001-03 for LEAF-IR's earlier run).

## Why Q08 fails for any values: a match found by both tiers keeps only its text strength
Q08 on LEAF-IR: 10 result runs; text strengths all weak; meaning matches shown: 0. Its best meaning card (rank 1, score 0.54939) belongs to a run that also has text matches: the meaning pointer resolves to that run's text chunk (pointer rule, case 1), and toResult drops a meaning pointer that duplicates a listed text pointer. The design does not define this merge (implementation choice in IR-001). On Granite, Q08 escapes only because two other runs' meaning matches rate Fair.

